<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:content="http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/"><channel><title>Example Site — #performance</title><description>Posts tagged with &quot;performance&quot; from Example Site</description><link>https://visruthsk.github.io/website-theme/</link><item><title>Measuring the theme against astro-erudite</title><link>https://visruthsk.github.io/website-theme/essays/measuring-the-theme/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://visruthsk.github.io/website-theme/essays/measuring-the-theme/</guid><description>The same nine pages built with astro-erudite and with this theme: a third of the bytes, an earlier largest paint, and a later first paint on a really slow link.</description><pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;THIS CONTENT IS ENTIRELY LLM WRITTEN&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;drop-cap&quot;&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;opening-words&quot;&gt;his theme&lt;/span&gt; is built on astro-erudite and adds a build-time line breaker, margin notes and citations. &lt;span class=&quot;footnote-sentence&quot;&gt;I built the same nine pages with both and compared what a browser downloads, how soon it paints and what Lighthouse scores.&lt;sup&gt;&lt;a rel=&quot;footnote&quot; role=&quot;doc-noteref&quot; href=&quot;#fn:scope&quot; id=&quot;fnref:scope&quot; data-footnote-ref aria-describedby=&quot;footnotes&quot; class=&quot;footnote-ref&quot;&gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;summary&quot;&gt;Summary&lt;a data-heading-anchor=&quot;&quot; href=&quot;#summary&quot; aria-label=&quot;Link to this section&quot; tabindex=&quot;-1&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
