&lt;td&gt;84 to 100, median 99&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;100 on every page&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Accessibility&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;95 or 96&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;100 on every page&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Best practices&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;100 on eight pages, 96 on one&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;100 on every page&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;SEO&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;100 on six pages, 92 on three&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;100 on every page&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Blocking time&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;0 ms&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;0 ms&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Layout shift&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;0.000&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;0.000&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The scores are whole numbers and most are identical across the 11 runs, so a median says more than an interval would. On a desktop every page scores 100 on both themes except the note, where astro-erudite scores 99. The theme paints the two maths pages in 0.28 s against 0.60 s.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;real-throttling&quot;&gt;Real throttling&lt;a data-heading-anchor=&quot;&quot; href=&quot;#real-throttling&quot; aria-label=&quot;Link to this section&quot; tabindex=&quot;-1&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lighthouse’s default mobile score uses simulated throttling, which models the page load instead of slowing the browser. Applied throttling slows a real browser to the same 1.6 Mbps link and 150 ms round trips. I audited five pages 7 times each this way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://visruthsk.github.io/website-theme/measure-real.svg&quot; alt=&quot;Seconds until first paint with the browser really slowed, five pages: the theme is up to a tenth of a second faster on the home page and listing and four tenths to six tenths slower on the essay, the note and the story&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The two methods agree on the home page and the listing. On the essay, the note and the story the theme paints 0.4 to 0.6 s later. It scores 1 to 3 points lower on the note and the story, and 1 point higher on the essay, where astro-erudite shifts its layout (0.113 against 0).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The font preloads cause the delay. With them removed, the story’s first paint under applied throttling dropped from 2.01 s to 1.56 s, level with astro-erudite’s 1.58 s. Under simulated throttling the same change made it 0.45 s slower, from 1.05 s to 1.50 s. A preload starts a font as soon as the HTML arrives, which the simulation rewards because it charges for every round trip. On a real 1.6 Mbps link the roughly 50 kB of fonts compete with the stylesheets for bandwidth. Switching &lt;code&gt;font-display&lt;/code&gt; from &lt;code&gt;block&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;swap&lt;/code&gt; changed nothing (2.01 s against 2.02 s), so the invisible text is not the cost.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The theme keeps &lt;code&gt;block&lt;/code&gt; and the preloads because the line breaker measures paragraphs with the real font files, and text set in a fallback face would not fit its breaks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;whole-site-size&quot;&gt;Whole-site size&lt;a data-heading-anchor=&quot;&quot; href=&quot;#whole-site-size&quot; aria-label=&quot;Link to this section&quot; tabindex=&quot;-1&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Every file in each build:&lt;/p&gt;
